      "note": {
        "id": "note", "type": "note", "title": "How the loop runs", "enabled": true,
        "x": 100, "y": 800, "w": 700, "h": 400,
        "content": "The hollis ledger, through the forge service (tools/forge_service.py).\n\nOn Send: the accepted outbox is read -- Read File never shows rejected drafts -- and delivered to the forge. The forge recognises events it already holds (same id) and appends only what is new, so re-delivery is safe. The roster comes back as guidance: who is written, who is unreliable, who refuses. The reply is written to that paperwork.\n\nAfter the draft: extraction proposes ledger events -- a part granted, a grudge changed -- into the outbox. Staged only. Press Apply and the events are real; reject and they die unborn.\n\nNext Send, the accepted events reach the forge and the roster moves. Pell starts unreliable -- nobody wrote him down. Write him a part, accept the reply, and next turn he helps. The paperwork wins.\n\nSetup: python3 companion/forge_service.py --seed-from companion/npcs/  (port 8788). Authorize a JSON Workflow Data target named forge-outbox with initial content []."
      }
